hors of the works we read can often be “obscured not by a ...\"\n  }\n]', Action 1: '<plan>\nTo fact-check the citation, I need to verify the text quoted in the in-line citation against the actual text in the article by David Greetham, specifically on pages 45-46 of the journal \"Textual Cultures: Texts, Contexts, Interpretation,\" volume 3, issue 1 from 2008. The citation provides a DOI link, which suggests that the article may be accessible through Project MUSE.\n\nFirst, I will attempt to locate the article using the DOI link provided in the citation. If the article is available, I will extract the text from pages 45-46 to verify if the quoted text matches. If the DOI link does not directly lead to the text, I may need to use a search engine to find the article or its text.\n\nThe task requires a precise comparison to identify any mismatches, so accessing the exact pages mentioned is crucial.\n</plan>\n\n<action>\ntool: google_search\nparameters: {\"query\": \"doi:10.2979/tex.2008.3.1.44\"}\n</action>']\n[Observation 2: 'Tool 'url_text_extractor' executed.\nResult: {\n  \"url\": \"https://muse.jhu.edu/pub/3/article/240795/pdf\",\n  \"extracted_text\": \"%PDF-1.4\\n%��͵\\n1 0 obj << /Type /Catalog /PageMode /SinglePage /Pages 2 0 R /ViewerPreferences << /NonFullScreenPageMode /UseNone >> >> endobj\\n2 0 obj << /Type /Pages /Count 13 /Kids [ 6 0 R 28 0 R 66 0 R 74 0 R 78 0 R 81 0 R 85 0 R 95 0 R 101 0 R 106 0 R 110 0 R 113 0 R 116 0 R ] /Resources 3 0 R >> endobj\\n3 0 obj << /ProcSet [ /PDF /Text /ImageB /ImageC /ImageI ] >> endobj\\n4 0 obj << /Author (David Greetham) /Language (English) /Producer (Project MUSE) /Title (\\nUncoupled\\n: OR, How I Lost My Author\\\\(s\\\\)) /XMP-dc:Creator (David Greetham) /XMP-dc:Language (English) /XMP-dc:Title (\\nUncoupled\\n: OR, How I Lost My Author\\\\(s\\\\)) >> endobj\\n5 0 obj << /Type /Font /Subtype /Type1 /BaseFont /Helvetica /Encoding /WinAnsiEncoding /Name /HelvCBK~1758699003 >> endobj\\n6 0 obj << /Type /Page /Conte